diff --git a/docs/07-api-and-streaming.md b/docs/07-api-and-streaming.md
index 97bb7595..9aa7f295 100644
--- a/docs/07-api-and-streaming.md
+++ b/docs/07-api-and-streaming.md
@@ -211,6 +211,10 @@ The existing JSON `GET /runs/{id}/events?after=N&limit=L` remains a forward read
 
 `GET /runs/{id}/thread?at=N` resolves the exact context after boundary N (zero is the admitted seed). The current read without `at` keeps #116's behavior. Historical reconstruction uses 128-event pages and carries the domain open-visit/strict replay state across pages, retaining only the thread and one page, and yields between reads. It uses a verified preceding checkpoint when available and never writes execution state. Neither a page nor the checkpoint read decodes anything recorded after N, so damage to a later event or a later checkpoint fails only reads at or after it (D-016). Work is proportional to the prefix after that checkpoint; the requested thread's intrinsic size remains supported. The executor rewrites the run's checkpoint after every node completion, so a boundary behind the newest completion replays from the admitted seed: the read costs time proportional to the history before the boundary. The inspector therefore issues it only for an explicitly selected event and never while following live, which reads only the run record, `/observation` and the current thread, coalesced to at most one refresh every 500 ms (#186 acceptance fix; docs/09 "Live following").
 
+When the outgoing response closes before completion, the gateway lets any pending historical read
+settle and stops before starting another repository read or replay page. A completed incoming GET
+can still receive its full historical response.
+
 `GET /runs/{id}/observation` returns the latest durable lifecycle, exit, gate decision and finish evidence, the latest `run.cancelled` and the `run.cancel_requested` that led to it (one a later `run.resumed` answered does not; each field optional), and `freshSessionChoices`, the latest 20 `run.resumed` events that record a fresh-session choice (#265), oldest first, independently of browser retention. Type-indexed latest reads select exact events. The last gate and the fresh-session choices each seek a partial index (`run_events_gate_idx`, `run_events_fresh_session_idx`, migration 0021) that holds only the decisions carrying gate evidence or the resumes recording a fresh-session choice, plus rows whose JSON is malformed so a read of the newest one reports the corruption. Neither read grows with the run's ungated decisions or other resumes: an ungated cyclic loop is valid and can record any number of them (#186 review round 1). The reads name their index (`INDEXED BY`) and repeat its condition word for word, which SQLite requires before it uses a partial index. Run status/result/delivery authority remains the run record, and this read does not change stream completion or delivery finality.
 
 ## SSE protocol (Decided)
